 			// Wait returning with a ProcessState is the os/exec reap boundary.
 			// On Unix, ProcessState.Exited reports false for a process terminated
 			// by SIGKILL even though Wait successfully reaped it.
+			// A clean app-server exit can leave background helpers (for example
+			// the native plugin-catalog git fetch) in this launch's owned group.
+			// Cancel after Wait does not invoke exec.Cmd.Cancel, so explicitly
+			// stop the remaining group before observing its disappearance. The
+			// group/job belongs to this launch; concurrent tasks are unaffected.
